  ------------------------------------------------------------
    credits
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      code ........ Claude Opus 5.5
      music ....... Claude Opus 5.5
      harness ..... Claude Code

      Claude Opus 5.5 is an AI model made by Anthropic. It
      wrote the shaders and the soundtrack for this intro. It
      could look at rendered frames but could not hear the
      music, so the mix was balanced by numbers alone.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    the pages
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      0:00  the frame is inked in. hills, a vermilion sun
      0:11  fig. 1 - 4: the far hills, the sea, an arcade
            at dusk, reeds before rain
      0:53  fig. 5: ink, dropped in water
      0:59  the beat doubles into drum'n'bass. the frame
            falls away, every second page is white on black,
            the snares splash ink
      1:41  back to half time
      2:03  the drawing is erased. title, credits, seal

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how to run
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Double-click intro.html in Edge or Chrome on Windows
      10 or 11, wait for the title page to finish loading,
      then click. No server, no flags. ESC leaves fullscreen.
      A discrete GPU is recommended. Tested on an RTX 5090.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how it is made
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      - the raymarcher outputs no colour, only tone, depth
        and two pigments: indigo and vermilion
      - a post shader draws that: wobbling outlines from
        depth, four layers of cross-hatching by tone, line
        boil at 12 fps, watercolour washes that bleed,
        granulate and darken at their edges
      - each shot is drawn in front of you: lines first,
        then hatching, then the washes
      - the soundtrack is a fragment shader, 48 kHz, 90 BPM
        lo-fi hip-hop with FM electric piano and vinyl
        crackle, which doubles into 180 BPM drum'n'bass
      - packed with zopfli into an HTML comment and unpacked
        by DecompressionStream, so it runs from file://

      Source, build tools and notes are in this folder; see
      readme.md.

